    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "frequently tested: Classifying bodies like NITI Aayog, NHRC, CVC, and UIDAI into Constitutional, Statutory, or Executive categories.",
        "Remember that NITI Aayog is an executive (non-constitutional, non-statutory) body formed via a Cabinet resolution on January 1, 2015.",
        "Constitutional provisions and corresponding article numbers for key statutory versus constitutional bodies are commonly matched in preliminary exams."
      ],
      "id": "l23g0ey"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their power, authority, and status directly from specific articles of the Constitution of India.",
        "Statutory bodies are established through acts passed by Parliament or State Legislatures.",
        "Executive bodies are created via an executive resolution passed by the Cabinet without legislative enactment.",
        "Any modification to the status or structure of a constitutional body requires a constitutional amendment under Article 368."
      ],
      "id": "s8s5z76"
    }
